New trailer slices into the combat, world, lore and features coming to Marvel’s Wolverine September 15.
Marvel&#8217;s Wolverine: Details on Logan’s mutant abilities, game features, and more
Today, we’re stoked to share with you our Features Trailer for Marvel’s Wolverine ! Narrated by Liam McIntyre, who plays James “Logan” Howlett, here’s a slice of what’s coming to the game on September 15&#8230; that’s just a few short weeks away!&nbsp; &nbsp;
Marvel’s Wolverine features fast, fluid, and ferocious combat with an emphasis on aggressive momentum. It’s all about getting in close and laying into enemies with everything you’ve got: claws, kicks, barrages, and critical strikes to start things off.
Evolve with Adaptations that amplify Logan’s momentum on the battlefield. Absorb more bullets, increase Rage effectiveness, expand parry windows, or straight up terrorize foes during mid-fight. This only scratches the surface; there are dozens of Adaptations to tune to your playstyle.&nbsp; &nbsp;
Go even further with Rage, a three-tiered pool of adrenaline that leans into survivability, resilience, and fury&#8230; in that order. Make a last stand against the odds and fight another day, or go berserk and kill without mercy to sustain Logan’s Rage. &nbsp;
Marvel’s Wolverine features an original story that will take Logan to places around the world, but things get dicey. Bolivar Trask is hellbent on executing his plans against mutantkind. It’s up to Logan and Jean Grey, alongside members of Team X, to sever his plans before it’s too late. In a world with too few mutants to form safe havens or organized heroic ensembles: this is a critical moment for mutant survival.
And while you’re out travelling the world, testing your battle skills against villains like Omega Red and Deathstrike, make sure to chop it up with your crew or take a detour between encounters: use senses to seek out Nightmare Doors to complete a variety of combat and traversal challenges; sniff out collectible whisky bottles to uncover Logan’s forgotten memories; or listen for material crates to craft suits inspired by comics, movies, animation, and more.&nbsp;
So, check out the trailer and read on for additional insights.&nbsp;
